		"nodes": {
			"19": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "ATTACK RELEASE\nThe Attack Release node (AR for short) is an envelope. \nWhen triggered the AR runs from 0 to 1, the speed of this is set by the attack time. \nWhen the 1 is reached the value starts to decline back to 0, the speed of this is set by the release time.\n\nA trigger is used to either start, reset or force release the envelope. \nBy default the AR restarts on each trigger, but this can be disabled in the patch panel."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 164.9790802001953125,
					"width": 737.29931640625,
					"x": 501.169464111328125,
					"y": 63.52208709716796875
